# Copy to backend/.env  --  never commit the real thing.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED. A GitHub *classic* PAT with the `public_repo` scope and nothing
# else. This is not optional-but-nice: an unauthenticated client is capped at
# 60 requests/hour AND cannot download Actions logs at all, which is the one
# thing TraceCI cannot work without.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The placeholder below is deliberately not 40 characters and not `ghp_`-
# prefixed. An earlier version used `ghp_xxxxxx...` padded to the real length,
# which is a plausible-looking string that survives a glance and then fails
# with a bare `401 Bad Credentials` twenty minutes later. Make placeholders
# impossible to mistake for values.
GITHUB_TOKEN=PASTE_YOUR_CLASSIC_PAT_HERE

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed for scripts/run_agent.py (the fast CLI loop). The web app is
# BYOK: the key arrives in the request body and is never read from here.
# The CLI checks TRACECI_API_KEY first, then the provider-specific names.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A FREE Groq key is the default and is enough to run everything:
#   https://console.groq.com/keys   (starts with gsk_)
TRACECI_API_KEY=PASTE_YOUR_GROQ_KEY_HERE
TRACECI_MODEL=groq-llama-3.3-70b
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
TRACECI_DB=./traceci_checkpoints.sqlite
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,https://your-app.vercel.app
